{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Of this red, red stuff.</b> The stew was very red — either from lentils, which are red, or because he seasoned it with red ingredients. Esav did not know what it was and called its name Adom (\"red\"); therefore they called his name Edom, for they mocked him that he sold a precious birthright for a mere stew, as it says: \"for the drunkard and the glutton shall come to poverty\" (Proverbs 23:21)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:34:48.920931294Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}